From f9c6ac90931f1614158791086e874cb10e9ac2c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: max rossi <113717219+maxr0ssi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:03:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] wined3d: Write streamed WoW64 buffer ranges straight
 into host buffer memory.

Add a small unix library to wined3d. On unmap of a DISCARD/NOOVERWRITE map in stream mode the CS
calls it once per range: it orphans the buffer for DISCARD, then maps just the range with
GL_MAP_UNSYNCHRONIZED_BIT, copies the application's bytes in and unmaps, on the host side where
the driver's pointer is addressable. Measured on macOS (Apple M3 Max): 0.3 us per upload+draw
natively, against 20-60 us for glBufferSubData() between draws and 70-140 us for a map through
opengl32's WoW64 copy. Falls back to glBufferSubData() when wined3d.so is not installed.
